      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The study details advancements in mRNA vaccine platforms, specifically focusing on optimizing lipid nanoparticle (LNP) delivery systems through modification of the ionizable lipid's pKa to enhance endosomal escape in murine models. Crucially, optimizing the N/P ratio demonstrably increases antigen protein expression within hepatic tissues, while the incorporation of pseudouridine-substituted nucleosides effectively mitigates innate immune sensing via TLR7 and TLR8 pathways. This molecular engineering strategy facilitates a sustained translational profile of the encoded antigen, representing a significant leap in vaccine immunogenicity.",
